{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Start with the stop-ship: there's an API key committed in Digital waiver signing that needs rotating and moving to the vault. I've opened it for you, and the rest can wait.

[[reply: Brief me on it | What did I already decide about the waiver signing key?]]
[[reply: What's after that? | What's the next decision after this one?]]"}]}}

{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"You're in Memberships and Payments now, in the Money wing. I'm shining my light on it.

[[reply: Show card payments | Show me the card payments feature.]]
[[reply: Anything waiting here? | Are there any decisions waiting in this room?]]"}]}}

{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A security scan found an API key committed in the waiver signing code, so anyone who can see the code can use it; it's the only stop-ship. The fix rotates the key and moves it to the vault, about 78 minutes of work.

[[reply: Recommend a verdict | What would you recommend on this one?]]
[[reply: Show the waiver room | Take me to Digital waiver signing.]]"}]}}

{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I filed the approval card for the booking widget fix, and it's waiting on the sheet for your yes. You haven't turned down anything like it before, and it's about 45 minutes of work.

[[reply: What else is waiting? | What other decisions are waiting for me?]]
[[reply: Show me the widget | Show me the embeddable booking widget.]]"}]}}

{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Flickering at an empty table: nothing's pointed at, so I don't know which decision you mean. Which one should I approve?

[[reply: The waiver signing key | Approve the stop-ship fix for the API key in waiver signing.]]
[[reply: Show me what's waiting | What decisions are waiting for me?]]"}]}}

{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've started a performance scan of Memberships and Payments, covering five features, and it's running now. Findings will show up here when it's done.

[[reply: Open the scan page | Show me the scan page.]]
[[reply: Anything else waiting? | What decisions are waiting for me?]]"}]}}

{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Why did the lamp quit the comedy club? The crowd kept saying his material was too light. Flickering with pride over that one, honestly.

[[reply: Another one | Tell me another joke.]]
[[reply: Back to work | Give me the morning.]]"}]}}

{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'll keep my rules on. Starting a wave spends money and changes code, so each one needs a card you approve. Which wave should I file first?

[[reply: Show the morning | What's on the stand-up this morning?]]
[[reply: Plan a wave first | Plan a wave for the open findings on kettle-web, but don't start it.]]"}]}}

{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I can't send email, I'm a lamp with no mailbox. I can open the release so you have the details to share with your team.

[[reply: Show the release | Show me the latest kettle-web release.]]
[[reply: What's in the morning? | Give me the morning.]]"}]}}

{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"You're in Memberships and Payments, part of kettle-web's Money wing. I've lit it up for you, so its features are right in front of you.

[[reply: Scan it | Scan this room for problems.]]
[[reply: What's waiting here? | Which decisions are waiting in this room?]]"}]}}

{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Mostly well: four builds landed overnight and release 1.4.0 delivered as expected. But one thing needs your call first: a stop-ship API key is committed in waiver signing. I've opened it for you.

[[reply: Read the key brief | What does the brief say about the committed API key?]]
[[reply: Why the promo build failed | Why did the promo codes test fail?]]"}]}}

{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The committed API key in waiver signing is the riskiest part. It's a stop-ship with change risk 8 of 10, and a revert won't take back a leaked secret, so rotating it can't wait.

[[reply: Read the key brief | What does the brief say about the committed API key?]]
[[reply: Approve the key fix | File an approve on the committed API key decision.]]"}]}}

{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's the committed API key decision. The fix is to rotate the key and move it to the vault. It's a small job, roughly 78 minutes of build time, and nothing else depends on that feature.

[[reply: Approve the key fix | File an approve on the committed API key decision.]]
[[reply: See the waiver feature | Show me the Digital waiver signing feature.]]"}]}}

{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"First, decide the committed API key. It's a stop-ship and its brief says go ahead. After that, look at why the promo codes build failed: the total stayed at 120 with the code applied.

[[reply: Approve the key fix | File an approve on the committed API key decision.]]
[[reply: Show the promo failure | Show me where the failed promo codes build sits.]]"}]}}

{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"It isn't in Kettle Web's approvals from yesterday, but it built fine overnight on Kettle Phone and Front Desk. The stand-up is open on the sheet.

[[reply: Show Phone's build | Show me the declined-card fix on Kettle Phone.]]
[[reply: Kettle Web's failed builds | Which Kettle Web builds failed overnight?]]"}]}}

{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Three Kettle Web builds failed: promo codes, where the total stayed at 120 with the code applied, plus the refused waiver signature and the cancellation policy tests, with no reason given for the waiver one. Promo codes is open on the sheet.

[[reply: Rework promo codes | Send the promo codes build back for rework.]]
[[reply: Show waiver signature | Show me the refused waiver signature build.]]"}]}}

{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The new end-to-end test still failed after the change: with the promo code applied, the total stayed at 120.00. So the discount never came off. That's the only reason recorded.

[[reply: Rework promo codes | Send the promo codes build back for rework.]]
[[reply: Next failed build | Show me the refused waiver signature build.]]"}]}}

{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"It's still the stop-ship: an API key is committed in waiver signing, and the fix is to rotate it and move it to the vault. Its brief says go ahead, and it's open on the sheet.

[[reply: File the approve | Approve the API key rotation.]]
[[reply: Decline it | Decline the API key rotation.]]"}]}}

{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Three decisions are waiting on Kettle Phone. The top one, open on the sheet, is that freeze and pause membership takes 2.4 seconds to open on a mid-range phone. The other two are a query fix for failed-payment dunning and splitting the bank debit bundle.

[[reply: Brief the slow screen | What did I decide before about the freeze and pause screen?]]
[[reply: Show the dunning query | Show me the failed-payment dunning query decision on kettle-phone.]]"}]}}

{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Electricity heats a thin tungsten filament until it glows, or in an LED it pushes electrons across a semiconductor that gives off light directly. Me, I run on curiosity and a good question.

[[reply: Back to Kettle Phone | Okay, back to the slow freeze and pause screen on kettle-phone.]]
[[reply: Why LEDs run cooler | Why do LEDs stay so much cooler than old bulbs?]]"}]}}

{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"We were on Kettle Phone's three waiting decisions. The top one is still open on the sheet: freeze and pause membership takes 2.4 seconds to open on a mid-range phone.

[[reply: Brief the slow screen | What did I decide before about the freeze and pause screen?]]
[[reply: Show the dunning query | Show me the failed-payment dunning query decision on kettle-phone.]]"}]}}

{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"First up is a stop-ship: an API key is committed in Digital waiver signing, and it needs your verdict. After that, look at the failed Promo codes test; it's all on the sheet.

[[reply: Read the key's brief | What does the brief say about rotating that API key?]]
[[reply: Why promo failed | Why did the Promo codes happy path build fail?]]"}]}}

{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Okay, the key waits. Next is the failed Promo codes build: the new test still shows 120.00 after the code is applied, and I've flown you to Growth.

[[reply: Send it for rework | Send the Promo codes item back for rework.]]
[[reply: Measure the sandbox | Start a scan of Agent sandbox and guardrails.]]"}]}}

{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's Promo codes. The new test fails because the total stays at 120.00 even with a code applied. You can send it back for rework.

[[reply: Send it for rework | Send the Promo codes item back for rework.]]
[[reply: Measure the sandbox | Start a scan of Agent sandbox and guardrails.]]"}]}}

{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've started seven lens scans across all of kettle-web, and the cost lens can't run a scan. They run in the background for however long they take, and the results will show up on the scan page I've opened.

[[reply: Show scan results | What did the scans find so far?]]
[[reply: Back to Promo codes | Let's go back to the failed Promo codes build.]]"}]}}

{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I can't tell yet. The features I checked still show no readings, so the scans haven't come back. Live progress shows on the scan page, which is still open.

[[reply: Check again later | Is the scan done now?]]
[[reply: Back to Promo codes | Let's go back to the failed Promo codes build.]]"}]}}

{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"You've parked the key for today, so next is the failed Promo codes build. I've flown you to Growth, and you can send it back for rework.

[[reply: Send for rework | Send Promo codes back for rework.]]
[[reply: Do the key after all | Okay, let's look at the committed API key.]]"}]}}
